Reursion-> Has Choices + Decisions
1)DP = Yaha pe kuch optimal puchte hai + (Choices and Decisions)
2)Backtracking = Yaha mostly puchenge ki sare combinations batao
3)Divide and Conquer

BT= Control + Pass by reference

All questions of BT can be solved by recursion
but not vice versa(can be done but complex)

Backtrack is used to revert the changes in previous node if the current node gets incorrect value.
This has to be done coz of pass by reference use in BT. This is redundant if we use pass by value
Pass by reference makes it efficient.. otherwise if we use recursion of 2D array in each node there
will be multiple 2D arrays!


Recursion me ANS leaft node pe milta hai
BT me ANS ROOT node pe milta hai and since combinations are asked so we get ANS ON a path
Usually in BT Questions there are a lot of Choices due to which we have to apply
for loop on choices for(c in choices){
                        if()--> control (Eg. East West North South House in West , E N S can be controlled )
                     }

Identification->
1) Choices + Decisions
2) All Combinations /All Paths /All valid etc keywords are used, Agar Optimal puchenge
to DP ya Greedy lag jata hai but agar ALL pucha to BT lagega!
3) Controlled Recursion
4) Number of Choices very large that cant make Recursion Tree looks weirdly large
5) Size of Constraints  Eg input has a String of size n and 1<=n<=10^6
BT time complexity is usually exponential ie 2^N or N^D or N!
so the n they give will usually be single digit ie. 1<n<10 itna bada diya hai matlab samaj jao BT hai
Agar n double digit hai ie 1<n<20 then well have to do optimal by DP
6)Dont be Greedy- Kabhi kabhi optimal puchte hai but DP mat lagana, DP tab lagegi jab koi choices bar bar arai hai
why greedy?
Eg largest in kth swap... 1234567 hum grredy hoke 1 for loop laga dete hai 4 baar swap karlo
but hume solution long term ke lie chaiye. Coz this greedy approach will fail for 4577.
Agar duplicate hai to greedy nai legegi varna lag jaegi.
islie kabhi kabhi BT ke problems Greedy se hojate hai but agar duplicate hai to Greedy nai lagegi
compulsory humko sab combinations try karne padenge.
Dusra tarika hai ki constraints dekho BT aur greedy ka zameen asman ka farak hoga


General code-
1)Usually BT method is void.
2)Base condition in BT usually call another function which returns boolean
    void BT(){
        if(isSolved()==True){-->Base Condition
            print or save the correct path or ans in vector. So if vector is pass by references then return type can be void
            no need to do all this for java. By default put void
            Adjust this as per question...
        }
    }

3) As per Identification step 4) choices are large
hence for(c in all choices){
    solve()--> recursion function
}

4) AS per Identification step 3) controlled recursion
90% questions will need control, 10% no need as it will require all choices
    if(choice/isValid== TRUE){
        Only then CALL function solve
    }

--PSEUDO CODE--
    void solve(&variable){
        if(isSolved)== true---> Base
            print

        for(c in all choices){
            if(isValid()==true)-->control
                changes in variable
                solve(changed variable)
                revert back above change
        }
    }
    return


Dimag kisme lagana hai ?
isSolved,
c in all choices
isValid